book><name>KAWAHARA, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIMURA, JUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>USHIJIMA, HIDETO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Liposomes having drugs encapsulated therein which have a positive targeting effect, surely remain stable in the blood and are efficaciously usable in diagnosing and/or treating diseases in association with the production of proteoglycans, in particular, kidney diseases, characterized in that the membrane components thereof comprise (1) a basic compound charged positively within the physiological pH range, (2) a lipid derivative of a hydrophilic polymer, and (3) a lipid constituting the liposomes, and the composition ratios of these components are as follows: the content of the component (1) ranging from 1 to 20 % by mol based on the component (3), and the content of the component (2) ranges from 0.2 to 5 % by mol based on the sum of the components (1) and (3).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des liposomes dans lesquels sont encapsulés des médicaments et qui présentent un effet cible positif, demeurent absolument stables dans le sang et peuvent être utilisés effacement pour établir le diagnostic et/ou pour le traitement de maladies liées à la production de protéoglycanes, en particulier les affections rénales. Ces liposomes sont caractérisés en ce que leurs constituants membranaires présentent (1) un composé de base chargé positivement, se situant à l'intérieur de la plage de pH physiologique, (2) un dérivé lipidique d'un polymère hydrophile, et (3) un lipide constituant les liposomes. Les rapports de composition de ces constituants sont les suivants: la teneur en constituant (1) est comprise entre 1 et 20 % en mole, par rapport au constituant (3), et la teneur en constituant (2) est comprise entre 0,2 à 5 % en mole par rapport à la somme des constituants (1) et (3).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>